Array.prototype.splice is a list mutation that takes the index and a length, and removes that many items from the array. It also returns an array of what it removed.

```js
const arr = [1, 2, 3];

const removed = arr.splice(1, 1);  // removes one item starting at index 1
// arr is now [1, 3]
// removed is [2]

arr.splice(0, 2, 'a', 'b');       // deletes two items and inserts two
// arr is now ['a', 'b', 3]
```

Pushing or spreading it into another array is a common way to copy it instead of mutating:

```js
const copy = [...arr];
```
